                                "example_id": "ec19fec7-fca4-4463-a410-b6175adb7179",
                                "sense_id": "7fd1cd8b-df15-30ea-9925-803fbbbcd75e",
                                "text": "English and Kiswahili might be Kenya’s official languages, but pupils tumbling out of school and students in the university canteens chatter to each other in Sheng, to their teachers’ despair. A witty, cheeky, freewheeling Clockwork Orange-style brew of Kiswahili, English and indigenous Kenyan languages, with added dollops of reggae jargon, American slang, French and Spanish, Sheng originated in Nairobi’s Eastlands slums in the 1980s."
                            }
                        ]
